--- !u!114 &821215117603091682
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 5019777438702524035}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: ed860e60688109d4ea51abbeb306bdb2, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ProjectSpark.UI.VisualTeaching.SparkAILessonLibrary
  teaching: {fileID: 3951809580460111607}
  entries:
  - id: 01_circuit_basics
    tier: 0
    topic: Core Concepts
    summary: Learn what a circuit requires before expecting a component to operate.
    keywords: battery source current connection wire return path
    lesson: {fileID: 11400000, guid: b39d802adf475bb4d8ec150a8418288c, type: 2}
  - id: 02_ohms_law
    tier: 0
    topic: Core Concepts
    summary: Explore I = V / R and the limits of a simple resistive estimate.
    keywords: resistor formula voltage current ohm resistance
    lesson: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 65a1002b01c4bc447850901434bf7624, type: 2}
  - id: 03_led_polarity
    tier: 0
    topic: Components
    summary: Learn why a typical LED needs appropriate polarity and current limiting.
    keywords: led diode cathode anode forward reverse polarity
    lesson: {fileID: 11400000, guid: e4a5486ad172a074cbb983eabba7b2c3, type: 2}
  - id: 04_switches
    tier: 0
    topic: Components
    summary: Compare a disconnected branch with a verified conducting path.
    keywords: switch open closed conduction return
    lesson: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 69cae2ebf6a4c8844b822ee2f1277b20, type: 2}
  - id: 05_resistor_bands
    tier: 1
    topic: Components
    summary: Read two significant digits, a multiplier, and tolerance from a typical
      four-band resistor.
    keywords: resistor color bands brown black red orange yellow tolerance ohms
    lesson: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 54133fbd892966748b0079d264fd90f3, type: 2}
  - id: 06_current_limits
    tier: 1
    topic: Measurements
    summary: Learn current limiting without assuming which component the evaluator
      measures.
    keywords: milliampere safe current target min max resistor objective
    lesson: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 3ff4d28986d0c9746ae6028627eaeac9, type: 2}
  - id: 07_power_heat
    tier: 1
    topic: Thermal Behavior
    summary: "Understand P = V\xD7I, rating margins, and verified burn-state diagnostics."
    keywords: burn heat overload smoke thermal rated watts power
    lesson: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0de2525cbe650c24184cea5c866ce729, type: 2}
  - id: 08_short_circuits
    tier: 2
    topic: Fault Finding
    summary: Follow safe investigation steps without guessing which wire is responsible.
    keywords: short circuit bypass fault wrong wire overload
    lesson: {fileID: 11400000, guid: f823516699b03d842b40bffed0f5d396, type: 2}
  - id: 09_systematic_diagnosis
    tier: 2
    topic: Fault Finding
    summary: Work from power-source status through return paths to component measurements
      and target results.
    keywords: diagnose troubleshoot led objective failed power path
    lesson: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 6709ae36d53fa3a4eb056192b8cab1a3, type: 2}
